<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Patches ~ the Grimalkin, Kai ʻĀ's Lynx-Mount

''The mechanical seat'' (from `campaign/company-structure.mem`): a ''large grimalkin-lynx
mount, Level 2'' — hallmark/sidekick asset of [[kai-a|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/kai-a]]. Player control law: Kai runs
Patches ''when mounted action, scouting action, or companion spotlight applies''.

''The true name:'' ''Patches'' — named for Kai's real kitty at
home on Gaia. The hearth-law reads clean: a hallmark carries a name already fed and loved at
a real hearth, the way every lararium stabilizes through use.

''The Gaia bio:'' female · long-hair ''calico'' · ''Maine Coon''.

''The Elyncian manifestation:'' the home cat carried across whole, then grown along her own
grain — ''+grimalkin +lynx-kaiju''. The Maine Coon already stands halfway to lynx (tufted
ears, snowshoe paws, the great ruff, the shaggy storm-coat); Elyncia finishes the walk and
keeps going: a ''grimalkin'' (faerie-touched, threshold-mannered, a gaze that weighs you)
at ''lynx-kaiju'' scale — mount-sized trending monstrous, the companion of a Kaiju Stalker
carrying a thread of the kaiju register in her own frame. The calico patchwork rides at
that scale as ''territory-map coat'' — continents of orange, black, and white.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-word>>

!! The Word ~ what "grimalkin" carries

//(Provisional — folklore substrate for the table to draw on or ignore.)// ''Grimalkin'' —
grey + malkin — the old English fae-cat: the witch's familiar hailed on the heath ("I come,
Graymalkin"), the cat that outlives its keepers, the beast the parish half-fears and
half-feeds. In Elyncia's register that folds cleanly: a grimalkin-lynx reads as a
''faerie-touched hunting cat'' — tufted ears, threshold-manners, a gaze that weighs you —
grown to mount-size the way everything on the fae side grows when it decides a road needs
walking. Whether hers reads as familiar, mount, partner, or all three at once belongs to Kai.

<<~/ahu>>

